s747/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bgates747/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":8183,"digest":"sha256:d2c3fe4db80d77c3baa7058e94ef24be6b540bbd7adb03a1588a38075b98daf6","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-09T03:37:54Z","updated_at":"2026-11-09T03:37:55Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/bgates747/agon-vdplet/releases/download/v0.1.2-alpha/verification.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bgates747/agon-vdplet/tarball/v0.1.2-alpha","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bgates747/agon-vdplet/zipball/v0.1.2-alpha","body":"VDPlet Runtime **0.1.2-alpha** is a prerelease for coordinated application testing.\n\nThe shared firmware now includes the audited ESP-IDF4.4.6 UART receive-full recovery fix. The ISR publishes the full flag and disables RX interrupts under the same existing lock, preventing another core's recovery from leaving reception disabled. This is the exact minimal repair proposed in [Agon VDP PR354](https://github.com/AgonPlatform/agon-vdp/pull/354).\n\nFirmware configuration: classic ESP32; pixels, text96, borrowed colour rows and bounded READ_BYTES enabled. Async worker, overlap witness, quiet async polling, counted return and PCM sink are disabled. Product branding is0.1.2-alpha; public ABI and wire versions are unchanged.\n\nValidation:49 focused source/export/provider checks, maintained ASan/UBSan host suite and native firmware/link/disassembly checks passed. The repaired source is the actual linked UART provider; the original SDK UART object is excluded. This versioned image has not been run on hardware or an emulator. Historical private-image hardware results do not qualify this new composition.\n\nThis tag also publishes accumulated performance tooling, optional async source/qualification, engineering guidance and cross-project review records. Their inclusion does not enable those optional features or imply completion of every investigation.\n\nUse the versioned firmware asset and SHA256SUMS. Compressed ELF/map files and the manifest provide debugging and provenance. No bootloader/partition update is part of this release. Existing images are not automatically replaced; application migration and deployment remain owner-controlled.\n"}